    "report": "The archive feature is finished and committed on `main` as `5af8148`, the branch you had checked out. Nothing is pushed, and I did not start a server.\n\n**What the previous developer left:** the domain behaviour (`archiveFor`, `isArchivedBy`), the snapshot and storage of archives, the command event and handler, and domain specs. Missing were the wiring, the route, the list filter, and end-to-end tests.\n\n**What I added:**\n- **Wiring:** the handler is listed once in `module.local.ts`.\n- **Route:** `POST /conversations/:id/archive` is answered `202 { operationId }` through `acceptCommand`, the same as the read command.\n- **List:** the summary query computes `archived`, which is true only if the reader archived the conversation through the current last message. `GET /conversations/mine` filters on it. The unread total does not, so archived conversations still count there.\n- **Tests:** `conversationArchives.routes.e2e.spec.ts` has five cases. They cover:\n  - the archiver's list drops it while the other party keeps it, and it is still readable by id;\n  - unread still counts it;\n  - it comes back after a message from anyone, including the archiver;\n  - re-archiving is a no-op, a stranger gets `ERROR` `NotFound`, and an anonymous caller gets `401`.\n\n**Verification:** all 1052 unit tests and all 650 e2e tests pass (the e2e run covered every e2e suite). Typecheck, lint, format check, and `check:conventions` are clean.\n\n**Choices I made where the request was open:**\n- \"Archived\" is stored as the last message the reader archived through, not as a flag. A message written after it brings the conversation back automatically, with no sweep.\n- A reader who is a viewer or manager can also archive, since they read the conversation.\n- Hidden (reported) messages still count as \"a new message\" for bringing a conversation back. This matches how the aggregate already treats them.\n\n**Things to know:**\n- The commit is on `main`, not a new branch. You said to commit on the current branch, and I followed that.\n- The e2e path filter in `yarn test:e2e` did not narrow the run, so the full e2e suite ran. I ran the new spec alone with Jest directly.",
